Keep unchanged clients alive; hold references for in-flight old-generation calls, close only retired clients after completion/deadline, and handle add/remove views without replacing HTTP/OAuth infrastructure. Explicitly define removal/revocation in-flight behavior. Acceptance: unrelated long call completes through view edit, changed upstream drains, new calls to removed tools fail, and other users' sessions survive; no task/process leaks.
